## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a comprehensive CAPA program with cross-tenant isolation, region awareness, and automation for policy drift scenarios during canary deployments. It probes API design skills, containment strategies, and the ability to define measurable impact metrics.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence linkage to logs and traces
- Region-aware lifecycle with staged gating
- Automated rollback and cross-tenant isolation checks
- Lightweight REST API for CAPA management
- Production metrics to prove recurrence reduction and effectiveness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express sketch for CAPA creation
app.post('/capas', async (req, res) => {
  const { tenant_id, policy_id, region, evidence_logs } = req.body;
  const capa = await capaService.create({
    tenant_id,
    policy_id,
    policy_version: await policyService.getCurrentVersion(policy_id),
    evidence_logs,
    region,
    detection_ts: new Date(),
    status: 'open'
  });

  if (capa.severity === 'critical') {
    await rollbackService.trigger(capa.policy_id);
  }

  res.status(201).json(capa);
});

// Automated rollback endpoint
app.post('/capas/:id/rollback', async (req, res) => {
  const capa = await capaService.get(req.params.id);
  const previousVersion = await policyService.getPreviousVersion(capa.policy_id);
  await policyService.rollback(capa.policy_id, previousVersion);
  await capaService.updateStatus(capa.id, 'containment_complete');
  res.json({ status: 'rollback_complete' });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to scope a CAPA (Corrective Action and Preventive Action) program for edge-layer data exposure incidents, enforce policy across geographically distributed regions, and connect preventive actions to measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model design capturing evidence, headers, tenants, and logs
- Region-aware lifecycle with defined state transitions
- Canary rollout methodology with control-plane/data-plane separation
- Performance and privacy metrics tailored for edge environments

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model
const CAPA_STATES = {
  NEW: 'new',
  INVESTIGATING: 'investigating',
  ROOT_CAUSE_IDENTIFIED: 'root_cause_identified',
  REMEDIATION_PLANNED: 'remediation_planned',
  IN_REMEDIATION: 'in_remediation',
  VERIFIED: 'verified',
  CLOSED: 'closed'
};

class CAPA {
  constructor(data) {
    this.id = data.id;
    this.title = data.title;
    this.severity = data.severity;
    this.state = CAPA_STATES.NEW;
    this.evidence = data.evidence || [];
    this.headers = data.headers || [];
    this.tenants = data.tenants || [];
    this.logs = data.logs || [];
    this.traces = data.traces || [];
    this.region = data.region;
    this.createdAt = new Date();
  }

  transition(newState) {
    const validTransitions = {
      [CAPA_STATES.NEW]: [CAPA_STATES.INVESTIGATING],
      [CAPA_STATES.INVESTIGATING]: [CAPA_STATES.ROOT_CAUSE_IDENTIFIED, CAPA_STATES.CLOSED],
      [CAPA_STATES.ROOT_CAUSE_IDENTIFIED]: [CAPA_STATES.REMEDIATION_PLANNED],
      [CAPA_STATES.REMEDIATION_PLANNED]: [CAPA_STATES.IN_REMEDIATION],
      [CAPA_STATES.IN_REMEDIATION]: [CAPA_STATES.VERIFIED],
      [CAPA_STATES.VERIFIED]: [CAPA_STATES.CLOSED],
      [CAPA_STATES.CLOSED]: []
    };

    if (validTransitions[this.state].includes(newState)) {
      this.state = newState;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

